__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage*
htmlcov/
.DS_Store
.private/
# best-engine writes the machine-specific chosen models here (per-machine, never commit)
llm.engine*.yaml
# Real cloud API keys (see settings.yaml.example); os_helper.get_config reads
# this from the current directory in llm._cloud_api_key. Never commit it.
settings.yaml

# Runtime working directory bind-mounted by docker-compose.yml. Whatever the
# container writes lands here on the host; none of it belongs in the repo.
data/

# Rendered video. The film is an OUTPUT: `assets/film/film.yaml` is a ledger of
# what it renders FROM, and its own comment says the film "can be rebuilt from a
# clone, which is the whole point of the ledger". Shipping the render as well
# put 1.6 MB of derived bytes in every clone forever, for a file no test opens
# and no CI step reads. Keep the composition, the captions, the poster and the
# ledger; regenerate the rest.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.m4v
